What is Portable Long-term EEG?
Portable Long-term EEG devices represent a revolutionary shift in neurological diagnostics, enabling continuous brain activity monitoring outside clinical settings. Unlike traditional EEG systems constrained to short hospital sessions, these ambulatory devices can record electrical brain waves for days or weeks while patients maintain normal daily activities. This extended monitoring capability is particularly transformative for capturing intermittent neurological events that standard EEGs might miss.
The technology comes in both wired and wireless configurations, with wireless options gaining significant traction due to improved patient comfort and data transmission capabilities. Modern portable EEGs integrate advanced features including cloud connectivity, extended battery life, and sophisticated signal processing algorithms, making them indispensable tools for diagnosing conditions like epilepsy, sleep disorders, and other neurological abnormalities.
